      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-12T21:41:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Will this stay in the Android downstream copy of crosvm only? If it\u0027s meant to be added to upstream crosvm, I don\u0027t think this will fly since PIDs/TIDs on general Linux can be larger than 16 bits, and I think this is true even on Bionic - bionc/README.md says \"*32-bit* bionic requires PIDs less than 65536\", but doesn\u0027t say anything about 64-bit bionic.\n\nIt is probably simpler to just send a separate 32-bit tid unless there\u0027s a really strong reason to pack everything into a single u32 (assuming we get to make up the protocol and it\u0027s not something that is already defined elsewhere).",
      "revId": "cb8566a44d56fa8ce154cf66e106829dc73618d7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
